1
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:14,000
A drug-fuelled road trip in the 60s

2
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Magic Trip: Ken Kesey's Search for a Kool Place is a
documentary, music film directed by Alison Ellwood.

3
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:30,000
A freewheeling portrait of Ken Kesey and the Merry Prankster’s fabled
road trip across America in the legendary Magic Bus.

4
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:38,000
In 1964, Ken Kesey, the famed author of “One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest,” set off on a
legendary, LSD-fuelled cross-country road trip to the New York World’s Fair.

5
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:46,000
He was joined by “The Merry Band of Pranksters,” a renegade group of counterculture truth-seekers, including Neal Cassady, the
American icon immortalized in Kerouac’s “On the Road,” and the driver and painter of the psychedelic Magic Bus.

6
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:54,000
Self, played by Ken Kesey.

7
00:49:56,000 --> 00:50:02,000
Self (archive footage), played by Jerry Garcia.

8
00:57:04,000 --> 00:57:10,000
Self, played by Neal Cassady.

9
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:18,000
Self (archive footage), played by Phil Lesh.

10
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
Self (archive footage), played by Bob Weir.

11
01:18:28,000 --> 01:18:34,000
Ken Babbs (born January 14, 1936)  is a Merry Prankster who
became one of the psychedelic leaders of the 1960s.

12
01:25:36,000 --> 01:25:42,000
He along with best friend and Prankster leader, Ken
Kesey, wrote the book Last Go Round.

13
01:32:44,000 --> 01:32:50,000
Babbs is best known for his participation in the
Acid Tests and on the bus Furthur.

14
01:39:52,000 --> 01:39:58,000
The film explores themes of biography, based on true
story, road trip, woman director.
